[FILE]\"','    - .theseus/adapter/environment.md').replace('    - \"[WHAT MUST NOT CHANGE]\"','    - No change to the project\\'s source code')\ns=s.replace('  commands: []','  commands:\\n    - curl -fsS http://localhost/healthcheck')\ns=s.replace('## Essential context\\n','''## Essential context\nDone by an operator (or an executor allowed to run `sudo -u postgres psql`, read /etc and /var/lib/dpkg), not by a measurement executor. State on 2026-11-02: euro-office-documentserver 9.3.7-1 is `half-configured`; postgresql, redis-server and rabbitmq-server (now installed) start with `service`; the postinst stops at \"can't connect to postgresql database\" because the DB role/database do not exist; `update-notifier-common` postinst fails (`import apt_pkg`, Python mismatch); debconf needs `DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive`; nginx failed to start. Steps: create role/DB from the package config, `dpkg --configure -a`, set ALLOW_PRIVATE_IP_ADDRESS, start nginx/supervisor, verify /healthcheck, then rewrite environment.md with the real procedure (the single `apt-get install` line is wrong).\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='.theseus/spawn/PKT-0016-make-pkt-0016-acceptance-require-real-latency-nu.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('    - \"[FILE]\"','    - .theseus/queue/in-progress/PKT-0016-break-down-client-open-and-co-edit-latency-on-realistic.md').replace('    - \"[WHAT MUST NOT CHANGE]\"','    - No change to the project\\'s source code')\ns=s.replace('  commands: []','  commands:\\n    - theseus validate')\ns=s.replace('## Essential context\\n','''## Essential context\nReviewer of PKT-0016 asked that its acceptance require real numbers; `test -s baseline.md` passes without any measurement. The executor may not edit packet frontmatter. Replace it with e.g. a check that a results file under .theseus/oracle/perf/ (client-breakdown JSON) exists and holds numeric open-time phases for docx/xlsx/pptx. Depends on the provisioning packet.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nls .theseus/queue/in-progress/","description":"Fill in spawn requests"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":26,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I couldn't do PKT-0016 again: no latency measurements were taken. The Document Server still won't start because I wasn't allowed to create its PostgreSQL user and database. The acceptance check (`test -s .theseus/oracle/baseline.md`) passes, but only because that file already has content, not because anything was measured.\n\n**What I got working:**\n- PostgreSQL and Redis start with `service`.\n- RabbitMQ was missing. `apt-get install -y rabbitmq-server` installed it and it now starts.\n\n**Where it stopped:** `sudo -u postgres psql -c \"CREATE USER ...\"` and `su postgres -c psql ...` were refused (\"requires approval\"). I didn't try to get around that. Without the database, the package's setup step can't finish, so the package is still `half-configured` and the server can't be checked or measured.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- You asked me to fix `environment.md` and make the acceptance check require real numbers. Both files are outside what this packet may change, so I filed two requests in `.theseus/spawn/`:\n  1. Set up the full stack and rewrite `environment.md` with the steps that actually work.\n  2. Replace PKT-0016's acceptance check with one that needs a results file under `.theseus/oracle/perf/` holding real timings for docx, xlsx and pptx.\n- `baseline.md` is unchanged. The Executor log and friction record are written, `theseus validate` reports 0 errors, and everything is committed as `13a9672`.\n\n**To unblock:** someone with `psql` rights needs to finish the first request, or the executor needs permission for `sudo -u postgres psql` and to read `/etc` and `/var/lib/dpkg`.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Measurement packets should only be handed out once the server's health check responds.\n- The one-line `apt-get install` in `environment.md` doesn't work on this machine. The real setup also needs the database user and database created, RabbitMQ installed, `DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive`, and a fix for the broken `update-notifier-common` setup.\n- `theseus packet new` only accepts these types: characterize, investigate, refactor, migrate, rewrite, interop, port-upstream.","ttft_ms":1392,"type":"result","duration_ms":78703,"uuid":"8b03a74c-4682-4666-98d6-8e659fd11453","ttft_stream_ms":817,"time_to_request_ms":332,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":217,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":20,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":20,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":21,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":151,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":244,"process_anon_mib_result":153,"process_peak_rss_mib":259,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2863,"process_wall_ms_turn":78702,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1275,"process_wall_ms_streaming":46333,"main_stream_count":20,"main_stream_event_count":988,"main_stream_chunk_count":530,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":6,"cpu_ms":19,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,